## Methodology

Passive subdomain enumeration, DNS resolution, HTTP probing and technology
fingerprinting, top-port service discovery, passive crawling, Nuclei
template matching (CVE / misconfig / exposed-panel / default-login), and
typosquat enumeration. Findings were correlated against a local CVE cache and
triaged for real-world impact.

## Scope & authorization

All activity was conducted under authorization reference **{{ auth_ref }}**
against the scope listed above. Every tool invocation is recorded in the
evidence manifest (`evidence/manifest.json`) with timestamp, SHA-256 hash,
and blast-radius classification.

## Limitations

- External / non-intrusive only. Internal, authenticated, and business-logic
  issues are out of scope for this checkup.
- Automated tooling produces candidate findings; a human should validate each
  before client remediation.
